                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>The Secretary of State’s Panel of Consultants on Disarmament met at Cambridge,
                    Massachusetts, June 19–21. J. Robert Oppenheimer, Joseph E. Johnson, and
                    McGeorge Bundy, the Executive Secretary, were present throughout. John S. Dickey
                    was present on June 19 and 20. Allen W. Dulles and Vannevar Bush were unable to
                    participate. The meetings were held mainly for the purpose of discussing general
                    aspects of the question of disarmament with a number of visiting experts. No
                    conclusions were formally recorded. Ten pages of minutes of the sessions,
                    prepared by Bundy, are in Disarmament files, lot 58 D 133, “Panel of Consultants
                    on Disarmament”.</p>
            </div>
